[h1]About[/h1]
Universum Infinitum - Planet Modifiers is a Stellaris mod that adds five new planet modifiers — extreme temperatures, absence of a magnetic field, a thin atmosphere, salinity, and swampland — each with its own icon and English localisation, weighted to match the vanilla v4.5 planet modifier pool.

[h1]Capabilities[/h1]
[list]
[*]Adds five new planet modifiers with distinct names, descriptions, and icons.
[*]Gates each new modifier with planet-class and star-system conditions so that it appears on thematically plausible worlds.
[*]Excludes mutually contradictory modifiers, so a planet never carries both a tidal lock and extreme temperatures, or two magnetic-field variants.
[*]Excludes the new modifiers from vanilla modifiers that already cover the same theme, so no duplicate concept enters the pool.
[*]Reproduces the vanilla v4.5 spawn conditions for the two vanilla modifiers it re-declares, changing only their exclusions.
[*]Scales every effect within the vanilla v4.5 band for comparable modifiers.
[*]Caps modifier accumulation per planet.
[*]Provides English localisation for every new modifier.
[/list]

[h1]Installation[/h1]
    [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2072966604][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hmlendea/readme-assets/master/badges/stores/steam-workshop.png[/img][/url] [url=https://steamcommunity.com:/linkfilter/?url=https://nexusmods.com/stellaris/mods/223][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hmlendea/readme-assets/master/badges/stores/nexus.png[/img][/url] [url=https://steamcommunity.com:/linkfilter/?url=https://github.com/hmlendea/stellaris-ui-planet-modifiers/releases][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hmlendea/readme-assets/master/badges/stores/github.png[/img][/url]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
This mod is compatible with Stellaris v4.5.* on all operating systems.

The subsequent languages are currently supported:
[list]
[*]English (en): Complete
[/list]

Translations are welcome. See the [url=https://steamcommunity.com:/linkfilter/?url=https://github.com/hmlendea/stellaris-ui-planet-modifiers]GitHub repository[/url] for the translation process.

Multiplayer sessions require the same mod version on every client, and divergent mod sets produce inconsistent presentation and statistics. Spawn chances are relative, so changing one modifier's weight shifts the effective probability of every other candidate, and modifier identifiers recorded in save files leave existing saves with dangling references when one is renamed or removed. The mod also references vanilla planet-class, star-class, and planet-modifier identifiers that it neither defines nor validates, so a host-side rename changes eligibility silently.

